int l = 0;
int r = n - 1;

while (l <= r) {
  // Scan right until finding an out-of-place value
  while (l <= r && predicate(arr[l])) l++;

  // Scan left until finding an out-of-place value
  while (l <= r && !predicate(arr[r])) r--;

  // Exchange out-of-place elements and advance indices
  if (l <= r) swap(arr, l++, r--);
}
```

Loop ends with `l == r + 1` and:

- `[0, l)` satisfies predicate
- `[l, n)` does not satisfy predicate

