  swap(arr, l, r);
}
```

At termination:

- `[lo, r]` is `<= pivot`
- `[r + 1, hi]` is `>= pivot`

Comment: `pivot` must be taken from the partitioned segment for the inner loops to safely terminate.

```c
int lt = 0;
int i = 0;
int gt = n - 1;

while (i <= gt) {
  if (arr[i] < pivot) swap(arr, lt++, i++);
  else if (arr[i] == pivot) i++;
  else swap(arr, i, gt--);  // don't increment i!
}
```

Note: When swapping an element greater than the pivot with `arr[gt]`, do not increment `i` because the newly swapped-in element has not been examined yet.

After each iteration:

- `[0, lt)`: known < pivot
- `[lt, i)`: known == pivot
- `[i, gt]`: unknown
- `[gt + 1, n)` known > pivot

At termination `i == gt + 1` and:

- `[0, lt)`: known < pivot
- `[lt, gt]`: known == pivot
- `[gt + 1, n)`: known > pivot
